#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:1
msgid "Tile Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:3
msgid ""
"A Tile kernel works on whole tiles and never names a thread. A SIMT function "
"works on one element from one thread. A **tile library** joins the two. It "
"packages Rust device functions so the Tile compiler can call them from "
"inside a cuTile kernel, once per element or once per warp, and link them "
"into the kernel's cubin. The Rust side is `#[tile_export]`, the packaging is "
"`cargo oxide tilelib`, and the caller is cuTile Python's `foreign_call` "
"today, with [cutile-rs](https://nvidia.github.io/cuda-rust/cutile/) to "
"follow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:11
msgid ""
"#[tile_export(tile_shape = 128)]\n"
"pub fn relu(x: f32) -> f32 { .. }                     your Rust function\n"
"        |\n"
"        |  cargo oxide tilelib <crate> --arch sm_120\n"
"        v\n"
"<crate>.ltoir          device code     void relu_impl(float x, float "
"*relu_out)\n"
"<crate>.iface.tilebc   declaration     @relu(tile<128xf32> in, tile<128xf32> "
"out) -> tile<128xf32>\n"
"<crate>.impl.tilebc    implementation  @relu_impl implements @relu, one "
"invocation per element\n"
"        |\n"
"        |  tileiras --preview-create-tile-lib       (CUDA 13.5 or newer)\n"
"        v\n"
"<crate>.tilelib\n"
"        |\n"
"        |  tp.foreign_call(symbol_name=\"relu\", ...)   inside a cuTile "
"kernel\n"
"        v\n"
"the Tile compiler links relu_impl into the kernel's cubin\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:31
msgid ""
"[Kernels and Device Functions](../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-"
"functions.md) covers `#[device]` and the LTOIR route to CUDA C++. A tile "
"library is the same route with the Tile compiler as the caller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:40
msgid ""
"The direct-linkage path. cuda-oxide ships the code (LTOIR) and two "
"descriptions (interface and implementation bytecode); tileiras packs them "
"into one `.tilelib`, and a Tile kernel calls the Rust function from inside "
"its body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:46
msgid "Writing an export"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:48
msgid ""
"Put `#[tile_export(tile_shape = N)]` on an ordinary function. `N` is the "
"tile size the caller will pass. The function stays as written, so the rest "
"of your device code keeps calling it. The attribute adds two items next to "
"it: an `extern \"C\"` implementation on the native SIMT ABI, named "
"`<name>_impl` by default, and a host-only description that the compiler "
"writes out as JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:54
msgid ""
"The [`tilelib_relu`](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/tree/main/cuda-"
"oxide/crates/rustc-codegen-cuda/examples/tilelib_relu) example exports three "
"functions, and this chapter follows them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/tile-libraries.md:58
msgid ""
"use cuda_device::{tile_export, warp};\n"
"\n"
"/// Elementwise `max(x, 0)`.\n"
"#[tile_export(tile_shape = 128)]\n"
"pub fn relu(x: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"    if x > 0.0 { x } else { 0.0 }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"/// Scale a tile in place. The cuTile side knows it as `scale_in_place`.\n"
"#[tile_export(\n"
"    tile_shape = 128,\n"
"    name = \"scale_in_place\",\n"
"    symbol = \"scale_in_place_impl\"\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn scale(x: &mut f32, factor: f32) {\n"
"    *x *= factor;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"/// Sum over the 32 lanes of each warp; every lane gets the warp total.\n"
"#[tile_export(tile_shape = 128, sync = \"warp\")]\n"
"pub fn warp_sum(x: f32) -> f32 {\n"
"    let mut total = x;\n"
"    let mut offset = 16;\n"
"    while offset > 0 {\n"
"        total += warp::shuffle_xor_f32_sync(u32::MAX, total, offset);\n"
"        offset /= 2;\n"
"    }\n"
"    total\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

